          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I’ll include that too. To make \\(A\\) itself the input of the transform, we can move the Laplacian onto the kernel by integration by parts on \\(r\\ge1\\). This produces an explicit boundary constant \\(1/16\\), which I’ll retain in the formula and record alongside the direct Laplacian representation."
