      "msg_057d9eb180a8d853016ae21e80f89081958c5e25fa891d9ffc": {
        "id": "msg_057d9eb180a8d853016ae21e80f89081958c5e25fa891d9ffc",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg_057d9eb180a8d853016ae21e80f89081958c5e25fa891d9ffc",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1793203841.006,
          "update_time": 1793203850.554,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Created [working change note 01](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/book/changes/01_GENERATING_FUNCTIONS_AND_KERNEL_CHANGE_WORKING_NOTE_20261028.md). It records both requests and will accumulate our proposed revisions. **The manuscript is unchanged.**\n\nStarting with\n\\[\nA(r)=\\sum_{n\\ge1}e^{-\\pi n^2r^2},\n\\qquad \\Theta(r)=1+2A(r),\n\\qquad \\Delta_3=\\frac{d^2}{dr^2}+\\frac2r\\frac d{dr},\n\\]\nthe direct formula is\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nH(t,z)=\\frac1{16}\\int_0^\\infty\ne^{\\frac t4(\\log r)^2}\\,\nr^{\\frac32+\\frac{iz}{2}}\\,\n\\Delta_3\\Theta(r)\\,dr.\n}\n\\]\nReplacing \\(\\Delta_3\\Theta\\) by \\(\\Delta_3A\\) changes the prefactor to \\(1/8\\). This keeps the generating function, Laplacian, time weight, and spectral phase visible.\n\nTo make **\\(A\\) itself the input of a kernel transform**, integration by parts gives\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nH(t,z)=\\frac1{16}+\\int_1^\\infty A(r)\\,\\mathcal K_t(z,r)\\,dr,\n}\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\mathcal K_t(z,r)=\n\\frac14\\frac d{dr}\\left[\nr^2\\frac d{dr}\\left(\ne^{\\frac t4(\\log r)^2}r^{-1/2}\n\\cos\\!\\left(\\frac z2\\log r\\right)\n\\right)\\right].\n}\n\\]\n\nHere the derivatives and time dependence belong to the kernel. The constant \\(1/16\\) is the boundary contribution at \\(r=1\\), obtained from\n\\[\nA'(1)+\\tfrac12A(1)=-\\tfrac14.\n\\]\nThe note includes the expanded kernel and boundary calculation. Both representations remain candidates for the revised exposition."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": true,
