            "parts": [
              "The lower limit \\(1\\) came from returning to the original half-line \\(u\\ge0\\), since \\(r=e^{2u}\\). I should have made that switch explicit.\n\nA full-space formula is available with the Laplacian transferred to an exponential kernel. To make it converge for every real \\(t\\), the input is \\(\\Theta(r)\\) minus its explicit background \\(1/r\\) inside the unit sphere and \\(1\\) outside. The same \\(1/16\\) boundary contribution remains."
