          "create_time": 1793204868.868,
          "update_time": 1793204871.753,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Yes—I’ll focus on \\(t=0\\). That permits a cleaner option: the smooth, positive profile \\(1+r^{-1}-\\Theta(r)\\) removes both the unit-sphere kink and the separate \\(1/16\\) term. Its kernel is a single power of \\(r\\), multiplied by \\(1+z^2\\). The tradeoff is that the integral converges in \\(|\\operatorname{Im}z|<1\\), which includes the whole real spectral axis."
