          "create_time": 1793205646.494,
          "update_time": 1793205657.128,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Saved both notes:\n\n- [Brainstorm08 — rescalings and flow comparison](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/brainstorm/08_ZERO_TIME_RESCALINGS_AND_FLOW_BRAINSTORM_20261028.md)\n- [Continuation09 — clean formulas for the next chat](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/brainstorm/09_GENERATING_THETA_AND_FLOW_CONTINUATION_20261028.md)\n\nThe cleanest rescaling I found at \\(t=0\\) is\n\\[\nV(r)=1+r^{-1}-\\Theta(r),\\qquad\nG(u)=\\frac12e^uV(e^{2u})\n=\\cosh u-\\frac12e^u\\Theta(e^{2u}).\n\\]\nBoth are smooth and positive. With \\(u=\\tfrac12\\log r\\), the fundamental relations become\n\\[\n\\boxed{(1-\\partial_u^2)G=8\\Phi}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n16H(0,z)=(1+z^2)\n\\int_{\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb S^2}\nG(u)e^{izu}\\,du\\,d\\sigma,\n}\n\\]\nwhere \\(d\\sigma\\) is normalized spherical measure. This retains a three-dimensional integral while making the kernel elementary. Its convergence domain is \\(|\\operatorname{Im}z|<1\\), including every real observation. The notes also compare the equivalent [standard Mellin formulation](https://dlmf.nist.gov/1.14.iv).\n\nFor the flow discussion, ordinary cylinder heat gives\n\\[\nH_s(z)=e^{-sz^2}H(0,z),\n\\]\nso it preserves zeros and permits recovery of \\(H\\). I also worked out a simple linear combination with Newman flow: it reduces exactly to a Gaussian factor, a spectral rescaling, and a reparametrized Newman time. That supplies a concrete benchmark for a more substantive unified flow.\n\nThe continuation records the remaining choices, particularly exact observation preservation versus preservation up to a known nonvanishing factor. **The manuscript remains unchanged.**"
            ]
          },
